odest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Ur Energy Inc is a micro-cap energy business with a $244M market cap on $27M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1027% over the past three years and -4% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -58% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 6% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $67M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -35.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 6.5% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 6.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Energy peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 271% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 69/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressu